    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2658" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annĭcŭlus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		annus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a year old</i>, <i>of a year</i>, or <i>a yearling</i> (not in Cic.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">freq. in Vulg.): nuces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 17, 2</span></i>
			 Schneid.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">taurus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 5, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vituli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Micah, 6, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agnus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. Ex. 12, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ovis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					Lev. 14, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. ib. 15, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 65</span></i>
			: virgo vix annicula, * <i><span class="en">Nep. Att. 19,
				4</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aetas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 9, 2 al.</span></i>
			</div>
